# Installed via `make cron-install` (see Makefile) — this file is the
# source of truth for *this repo's* cron jobs, not for the whole crontab:
# scripts/install-crontab.sh merges it into a marked block and leaves every
# other line alone, so jobs the user added by hand survive an install.
# Changes made directly inside that block in the live crontab (crontab -e)
# are still overwritten on the next install — edit this file instead. Jobs
# unrelated to this repo belong outside the block, where they are kept.
#
# The repo path / PUID / DATA_ROOT placeholders used below (see individual
# job comments) are substituted by `make cron-install` from this checkout's
# path and .env.shared (cron never loads .env.shared itself) — never spell
# them out literally in a comment here, `sed` rewrites the whole file,
# comments included (bug hit while adding this sentence on 2026-07-30).
MAILTO=""

# Nextcloud background jobs, every 5 minutes (occ background:cron via cron.php)
# the placeholder below is substituted by `make cron-install` with PUID from
# .env.shared — never hardcode a literal uid here. Guarded by
# require-running.sh so this is a silent no-op (no failed docker exec, no
# marker write) rather than an error every 5 min when the nextcloud stack
# is stopped. Success marker consumed by scripts/generate-dashboard.py's
# "Tâches planifiées" card (see cron_marker_age_seconds()).
*/5 * * * * __REPO_ROOT__/scripts/require-running.sh nextcloud/app && docker exec -u __PUID__ nextcloud-app-1 php -f /var/www/html/cron.php && date +\%s > __DATA_ROOT__/.cron-status/nextcloud-cron

# Weekly restic backup (Nextcloud DB dump + data + .env secrets + image
# digest manifest) — see scripts/backup.sh
# the placeholder below is substituted by `make cron-install` with this
# checkout's absolute path — never hardcode a literal path here.
0 3 * * 0 __REPO_ROOT__/scripts/backup.sh >> __REPO_ROOT__/sauvegarde/backup.log 2>&1

# Refresh the dashboard every 5 minutes — mainly to reflect healthcheck
# status (see CLAUDE.md) without waiting on a manual `make dashboard-refresh`.
# Success marker consumed by the "Tâches planifiées" card itself (see
# cron_marker_age_seconds()) — if this cron stops firing, the marker goes
# stale and the very next successful regeneration will show it in red.
*/5 * * * * python3 __REPO_ROOT__/scripts/generate-dashboard.py >> __REPO_ROOT__/dashboard/refresh.log 2>&1 && date +\%s > __DATA_ROOT__/.cron-status/dashboard-refresh

# Trigger recyclarr sync (manual mode, no internal scheduler — see
# arr/docker-compose.yml) then immediately reapply the Sonarr/Radarr
# quality-definition size overrides + Radarr language field that it just
# reset to guide defaults (see arr/recyclarr/recyclarr.yml and
# scripts/apply-arr-overrides.py). Chained in one crontab line rather than
# two separate schedules so the window where these settings are wrong is
# bounded by the sync's actual duration, not an estimated safety delay.
# Guarded by require-running.sh (needs both sonarr and radarr up) so this
# is a silent no-op rather than a failed docker compose run/docker exec
# every night when the arr stack is stopped. Success marker (only reached
# if all prior steps exit 0) consumed by the "Tâches planifiées" card (see
# cron_marker_age_seconds()).
0 0 * * * __REPO_ROOT__/scripts/require-running.sh arr/sonarr arr/radarr && make -C __REPO_ROOT__ recyclarr-sync >> __REPO_ROOT__/arr/recyclarr-sync.log 2>&1 && python3 __REPO_ROOT__/scripts/apply-arr-overrides.py >> __REPO_ROOT__/arr/apply-overrides.log 2>&1 && date +\%s > __DATA_ROOT__/.cron-status/arr-overrides
